    {"text": "September 9th, 1947. Harvard's Mark II computer, and one long day in its logbook.", "durationSeconds": 5},
    {"text": "At eight in the morning, the operators start an arctangent run.", "durationSeconds": 4.5},
    {"text": "By ten it stops, and the check passes.", "durationSeconds": 4},
    {"text": "At eleven they load the cosine tape for a sine check.", "durationSeconds": 4.5},
    {"text": "Twenty-five past three: a multi-adder test begins.", "durationSeconds": 4.5},
    {"text": "Then, at three forty-five, something is wrong in Relay number seventy, Panel F. It's a moth.", "durationSeconds": 6},
    {"text": "They tape it into the log: first actual case of bug being found.", "durationSeconds": 5},
    {"text": "The arctangent run restarts at four thirty, and at five, they close down.", "durationSeconds": 5}
